<title>GREECE: GREEK IONIAN BANK HAS NEW PRESIDENT.</title>
<headline>GREEK IONIAN BANK HAS NEW PRESIDENT.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The board of directors of state Ionian bank appointed Haris Stamatopoulos as the bank's new president replacing outgoing Panayiotis Korliras.</p>
<p>Stamatopoulos holds a Ph.D in economics from LSE and has worked for years at the central bank. He is a former general secretary of the commerce ministry.</p>
<p>He is also the president of Athens International Airport SA and a member of the sub-committee on foreign exchange policy of the European Monetary Institute (EMI), the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
